 var svg= mSVG(s)+'<div class="note">Three custody paths leave the plant: NGL product to the pipeline through the V-8000 pig launcher (ESD-8000 now flanked by manual double-block XV-8000A/B added this session, PDIT-8000 meter run, FQI-8000A totalizer \u2014 accumulates live off actual NGL rate, stops accumulating if ESD-8000 is closed); residue gas to sales through the V-8200 residue gas pig launcher (ESD-8207 flanked by XV-8207A/B, real DCS tag ESD-S207); and a 6\u2033 supplemental fuel-gas takeoff branch (ESD-8220A flanked by XV-8220A/B, real DCS tag ESD-S220A, normally closed on this model \u2014 click its "i" icon for the confirmed real 2-row interlock). Drain/vent connections are now shown at V-8000 and V-8200, standard requirements for pig launcher operation (receiving/launching a pig requires depressurizing the launcher barrel first). Correct residue order is F-6800 discharge -> 6-inch supplemental-fuel-gas branch -> PIT-8210A -> TIT-8210A -> FIT-8210A -> ESD-8207 -> V-8200 pig-launcher branch / off-site sales. Operator-verified snapshots: PIT-8210A 953.22 psig, TIT-8210A 97.07 degF, FIT-8210A 207.91 MMSCFD; later 2026-08-18 live calibration FIT-1045A 223.37 MMSCFD / FIT-8210A 209.00 MMSCFD. Simulator FIT-8210A practical maximum is 219 MMSCFD; current 12FZ starting point is FIT-1045A 205.37 / FIT-8210A 196.01 MMSCFD with natural fluctuation (9.36 MMSCFD net difference). The 223.37/209.00 point and typical 10-18 MMSCFD differences remain historical rather than hard limits; PIT-8200 953.7 psig. On the residue leg past the fuel-gas branch: PIT-8210A (952 psig, 1005 psig HI alarm, confirmed real), TIT-8210A (97\u00b0F, confirmed real), FIT-8210A (residue sales rate), then ESD-8207 into the V-8200 pig launcher, then PIT-8200 (953 psig, 1150 psig HI / 1200 psig HIHI-SD, confirmed real) just before the pipeline tie-in. On the fuel-gas branch: PIT-8220D (125 psig, 100/200/250 psig L/H/HIHI-SD, confirmed real \u2014 the HIHI only shuts the fuel gas system by closing ESD-8220A, it does not trip the facility). PIT-8220C (951 psig) sits on that same branch upstream of the takeoff. Requires Verification: ESD-8207 does not yet have a confirmed real interlock popup \u2014 the "i" icon is wired but will show nothing until real interlock rows are provided (don\u2019t confuse with the unrelated XV-6060 interlock on the Residue Comp. page, which was mis-referenced against this ESD in an earlier dictation and corrected). Click an ESD or manual block valve to open/close it \u2014 closing ESD-8000 or ESD-8207 stops that stream\'s totalizer. All PIT/TIT/FIT tags (except the totalizer) are click-to-trend.</div>'
