var CF_PID_M2140_12IA={"number":"020185-AE-DW-M2140","revision":"8","page":"1","title":"Product Heater / Trim Heater; P-1629 methanol injection and E-1225 trim reboiler","sourceFile":"2026-10-05 21-19.pdf","sha256":"9b9c1fee51fd1323b0d24f284ca2e5f891f63e8dff63238854cf8dfc2dd7b89f","issueMarking":"ISSUED FOR DESIGN","sourceRetained":false,"sourceStorageMode":"learn-only","reviewed":"2026-10-05","scope":"Targeted catch-up source review of major circuits and readable annotations; NOT exhaustive fine-valve/instrument transcription. No new geometry or controls from this sheet.","facts":[{"id":"identity","tags":["P-1629","E-1225"],"text":"The latest supplied M2140 page bears Revision 8 and the issue marking ISSUED FOR DESIGN. It shows P-1629 methanol injection and E-1225 trim reboiler; it is not an expander mechanical drawing. Preserve this issue status rather than calling it issued for construction.","location":"Title block and equipment headings","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"methanol","tags":["P-1629","TK-1640"],"text":"P-1629 methanol injection pump heading is 21 GPH at 2000 PSIG MAX. Suction originates at TK-1640/M2250 and passes the shown strainer/isolations. The discharge manifold has separate tubing continuations to E-1221, E-1222, LCV-1421A, PCV-1121A and E-1241, with individually shown branch isolation/checks. These are source circuit identities, not a newly implemented injection procedure or commanded chemical rate.","location":"Left-hand methanol circuit","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"pump_relief","tags":["PSV-1629","P-1629"],"text":"PSV-1629 shows SET at 1100 PSIG, BLOCKED DISCHARGE, 1-in MNPT x 1-in FNPT. Exact complete return/termination requires tracing the pump loop and vendor source; no external flare route or model relief setting is invented.","location":"PSV above P-1629","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"trim_process","tags":["E-1225","E-1223","T-1521"],"text":"440-14-in-HL-B0-LT-1.5-in-CU comes from E-1223/M2165 into the E-1225 process circuit. 441-14-in-HL-B0-LT-2-in-CU returns toward T-1521/M2150 and is labelled DO NOT POCKET. Low-point drain 2137 is separately shown. Process side remains separate from HMO.","location":"Right-side trim-reboiler process circuit","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"hot_oil","tags":["TCV-1225A","E-1225","H-7100"],"text":"H-7100/M2700 supplies the separate 10-in hot-oil branch through TCV-1225A (FC) and its station; 582 is the exchanger-side continuation and 583 is the hot-oil return via 2138 CSC to the off-page return. Controller TIC-1225A reads a process temperature signal. Drawing temperatures/valve markings do not rewrite the operating TIC-1225 calibration.","location":"TCV station right of E-1225","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"},{"id":"other_circuits","tags":["V-1421","E-1224","E-1223"],"text":"The sheet also carries the 405/406 dry-gas split, 434 cold-separator C2-rejection path, 438 side-reboiler return, 436 tower side-draw marked FREE DRAINING, and 590 dryout/air gas. Their linework is not part of the methanol or hot-oil circuit; off-page continuations must be kept separate.","location":"Left dry feed and lower reboiler continuations","status":"DRAWING_TRANSCRIBED / FIELD_VERIFICATION_PENDING"}],"lines":[],"valves":[],"instruments":[],"pending":["Targeted major-circuit review only; detailed all-item transcription, tiny notes and exact valve/instrument codes remain pending.","ISSUED FOR DESIGN marking is retained literally; confirm controlled current construction/as-built revision before field use.","P-1629 relief termination, vendor pump details, fine injection branch tags and all placement remain pending.","No source-only reference record in this review implies a newly built pump, valve or pipe."],"status":"SOURCE_IMAGE_REVIEWED / FIELD_AND_VENDOR_DIMENSIONS_PENDING"};
